;;; `ein solve --dump-answer` refuses a `.einb` — M1f **W43**, register row
;;; `W43/einb-dump-answer` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), filed by S1f.5.12's
;;; T1f.5.12.4 (2026-11-09).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two names, `a` and `b`, each seen, and `p` the relation a run may commit
;;; to: the candidates are `(p a)` and `(p b)`. One rule, `clash`, refutes the
;;; two together. So R is three states, ∅, {(p a)} and {(p b)}, and N is one
;;; set, {(p a), (p b)}, whose core is the two facts, refuted by `clash`: an
;;; answer directory with state files and a member of N with its core.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; AGENTS.md: *every command that takes a `.ein` path takes a `.einb` too,
;;; dispatching on the magic bytes*, and the user's rule is one tool,
;;; consistent answers: no two commands, or one command on two forms of one
;;; program, may disagree. A `.einb` stores its program, resolved and
;;; import-flattened, and every command reads it (W40's six rows), so `ein
;;; solve x.einb --dump-answer DIR` answers as `ein solve x.ein --dump-answer
;;; DIR` does: exit 0, R's three states on stdout, and `DIR` holding a state
;;; file for each, the stored program and then the state, and `nogoods.json`
;;; with N's one member, its core (p a) (p b) and its rule, `clash`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `ein solve` refuses the container before the run, exit 2, with `error:
;;; --dump-answer DIR: a .einb container carries no program source, and every
;;; file the answer directory holds starts with it — run it on the .ein`,
;;; where `ein solve` on the container without `--dump-answer`, and every other
;;; command, answers it (2026-11-09).

(relation p T :why "{?1} is picked")
(relation seen T :why "{?1} is seen")

(seen a)
(seen b)

(rule clash () :match (and (p a) (p b)) :assert (false)
  :why "a and b are not both picked")

(solve :hypothesis-relations (p))
